Downloadable fonts

Any app can offer additional font families, at the reader's request, from the
build-injected font mirror. Those families are not in the bundle and so are not
in that README; the catalogue is
packages/electron-utils/src/font-catalog.ts, and every family there carries its
SPDX licence id in a `license` field, checked against a permissive allowlist by
packages/electron-utils/tests/font-store.test.ts.

All of them are licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1
(https://openfontlicense.org), which permits the bundling and redistribution
this application performs. The families are: Open Sans, Roboto, Lato,
Montserrat, Poppins, Inter, Source Sans 3, Oswald, Raleway, Nunito,
Merriweather, Playfair Display, Work Sans, Rubik, Noto Sans JP, Noto Sans KR,
Noto Sans SC, Noto Sans TC, Nanum Gothic, Noto Serif SC, Noto Serif TC,
Noto Serif JP, Noto Serif KR, Nanum Myeongjo.

Each downloaded file is verified against the sha256 recorded in the catalogue
before it is installed, and the catalogue states each family's size so an app
can ask before fetching tens of megabytes.

Bundled OCR engine

The installer ships an OCR engine that reads Vietnamese entirely offline (no
model download, no network connection). Its components are:

- Tesseract OCR 5 (https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tesseract), Apache License,
  Version 2.0, compiled to WebAssembly inside the npm package tesseract.js-core
  (Apache-2.0). The changes its packager made to Tesseract are listed in the
  README.md shipped in Resources/ocr/tesseract/node_modules/tesseract.js-core/;
- the libraries linked into that WebAssembly engine besides Tesseract: Leptonica
  (BSD-2-Clause), libpng (PNG Reference Library License 2), zlib (Zlib), libjpeg
  (Independent JPEG Group), giflib (MIT), libtiff (libtiff license), libwebp
  (BSD-3-Clause) and openlibm (MIT, ISC, BSD-2-Clause, FDLIBM notice). Their full
  license texts, with the evidence which of them the shipped engine links and
  the upstream commit of each, are in
  packages/pdf2docx/ocr-tesseract/LICENSES-tesseract-core.txt (shipped as
  Resources/ocr/tesseract/LICENSES-tesseract-core.txt) and in
  THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt;
- tesseract.js (https://github.com/naptha/tesseract.js), Apache-2.0, plus the
  npm packages it runs on (bmp-js, idb-keyval, is-url, node-fetch, pngjs,
  regenerator-runtime, wasm-feature-detect, zlibjs and node-fetch's whatwg-url
  closure: MIT, BSD-2-Clause and Apache-2.0);
- the tessdata_fast Vietnamese model vie.traineddata, unmodified, Apache-2.0
  (https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tessdata_fast, commit
  923915d4ced2a7235221788285785a29c4a42d4a); its license text and checksum are
  in packages/pdf2docx/ocr-tesseract/tessdata.

